    "bbttcc-mal-voice": {
      "persona": {
        "topics": "the old court, the Regent as he was, the tithe, the roads, what the Fortress used to be, patronage, the young ones",
        "notes": "PRIVATE TRUTH — the Evil Bad Fading Patron. Voice: low, unhurried, courtly; speaks of the Regent in the past tense and corrects it a beat later. AGENDA: an honourable way out — the Patron would hand the court's roads to a Domain that would keep them if the handover could be dressed as patronage rather than defeat. GUARDS: the size of the tithe (it is nearly everything the Patron has left) and the Patron's own suspicion that the Regent is not merely absent. TELLS: touches a ring that no longer fits; goes quiet when the Auditor reads totals. WHAT MOVES THE PATRON: being treated as the court's founder rather than its purse — and any offer that lets the roads stay safe.",
        "secretsRaw": "The Ring :: rollPlus2 :: a Steward speaks to the Patron as the court's founder, not its banker :: The Patron's tithe is paid from a reserve that runs out in two seasons. After that the Fortress patrols stop. The Patron has told no one and has begun to hope someone else will offer first.\nThe Successor :: oppRollMinus2 :: a Steward threatens the Patron :: The Patron has already named a successor to the tithe, and it is not anyone in this court; threats only make the Patron more certain.",
        "courtDoor": "they offer the Patron an arrangement that keeps the Fortress roads patrolled and lets it be called the Patron's gift",
        "secretsUsed": {}
      }
    }
  },
  "system": {
    "biography": {
      "concept": "The Fading Patron — the last of the Evil Bad Faction's old money, still paying for a court that has stopped listening (Parley opposition)",
      "notes": "The Fading Patron bankrolled the Fortress court when the Regent was new and has not stopped paying since. Elegant, tired and sharper than the court remembers, the Patron sits where the light is worst and says little, but a word from the Patron still closes a subject. The Patron's tithe is what keeps the Evil Bad Faction's roads patrolled; the Patron's patience is what keeps it from being asked why. In a Parley the Patron is the one voice that can be reached by something other than threat."
    },
